<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <!-- This tells the browser what character set to use -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8">

  <!-- This helps the page fit correctly on phones and smaller screens -->
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <!-- This title shows in the browser tab -->
  <title>C++ Programming Language</title>

  <!-- This connects the page to our external CSS file -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
</head>

<body>

  <!-- Adds the shared header and navigation menu -->
  <%- include("partials/header.ejs") %>

  <main>

    <!-- Main introduction for the C++ page -->
    <section>
      <h2>What Is C++?</h2>

      <p>
        C++ is a programming language used when programs need to be fast and
        efficient. It gives programmers more control over memory and computer
        resources.
      </p>

      <p>
        C++ is common in video games, operating systems, embedded systems,
        browsers, and other software where performance matters.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Figure keeps the image and caption together -->
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/img/cppPage.jpg"
        alt="C++ programming code on a computer screen"
      >

      <figcaption>
        C++ is often used for programs that need high performance.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- This card keeps the original HW 1 information -->
    <section class="card">
      <h2>Common Uses of C++</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Game development</li>
        <li>Operating systems</li>
        <li>Embedded systems</li>
        <li>Browsers and performance-heavy software</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why C++ Is Important</h2>

      <p>
        C++ teaches programmers about memory, performance, and how software
        interacts with hardware. Learning it also helps students understand
        lower-level programming ideas.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- This section displays real data from the language-map Node package -->
    <section>
      <h2>Node Package Information</h2>

      <p>
        The information below comes from the
        <strong>language-map</strong> Node package.
      </p>

      <div class="card">

        <p>
          <strong>Language type:</strong>
          <%= cppInfo.type || "Not available" %>
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Common extensions:</strong>

          <% if (cppInfo.extensions) { %>
            <%= cppInfo.extensions.join(", ") %>
          <% } else { %>
            Not available
          <% } %>
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Common filenames:</strong>

          <% if (cppInfo.filenames) { %>
            <%= cppInfo.filenames.join(", ") %>
          <% } else { %>
            Not available
          <% } %>
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Aliases:</strong>

          <% if (cppInfo.aliases) { %>
            <%= cppInfo.aliases.join(", ") %>
          <% } else { %>
            Not available
          <% } %>
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Language color:</strong>
          <%= cppInfo.color || "Not available" %>
        </p>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Source used for the basic C++ information -->
    <section>
      <h2>Source</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more from
        <a
          href="https://isocpp.org/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Standard C++ Foundation
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- Adds the reusable footer -->
  <%- include("partials/footer.ejs") %>

</body>

</html>